--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0263df275083eba45b37ab9636c8dcbf, type: 3}
  m_Name: MAP-065_Archipelago
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  mapId: MAP-065
  displayName: Archipelago
  environment: Island Chain
  warfareFocus: Distributed Warfare & Naval Control
  executiveSummary: "Archipelago is a multi-island chain battlefield built for distributed warfare, naval control, amphibious maneuvering, and autonomous multi-node coordination. The terrain features scattered islands, coral shelves, deep-water channels, mangrove swamps, cliffside fortifications, fishing villages, and offshore naval platforms. The map emphasizes Obsidian Protocol\u2019s autonomous distributed-node logic, naval-air coordination, sensor-fusion across water and land, and logistics under fragmented terrain constraints. In AR (Nreal Light/Air), the map anchors at ~4\u20135 m viewing distance, covering a 10\xD710 m physical area representing ~1 km\xB2 of island-chain terrain. Key features include multi-island objective nodes, naval chokepoints, amphibious landing zones, and distributed control of sea lanes."
  designGoals:
  - name: Distributed Multi-Island Warfare
    description: Archipelago prioritizes simultaneous control of multiple islands, each with unique terrain, resources, and defensive positions. Victory depends on coordinated multi-front pressure.
  - name: Naval Control & Sea-Lane Dominance
    description: Deep-water channels, coral shelves, and narrow straits create naval chokepoints. Controlling sea lanes determines reinforcement speed and amphibious landing viability.
  - name: Amphibious Operations & Island Hopping
    description: Players conduct coordinated landings using amphibious armor, drones, and infantry. Beaches, mangroves, and cliffs create layered defensive zones.
  - name: Air Operations & Reconnaissance
    description: VTOL aircraft, drones, and long-range recon planes operate above the island chain. Airspace corridors between cliffs and offshore platforms define movement and targeting.
  - name: Autonomy & Distributed Node Coordination
    description: Autonomous units coordinate across multiple islands, selecting optimal nodes to attack or defend based on sensor data, enemy movement, and objective priority.
  - name: Sensor & Information Warfare
    description: Sea spray, humidity, thermal distortion, sonar scatter, and magnetic interference degrade sensors. Relay towers on cliffs restore clarity. Destroying relays creates blind pockets across the archipelago.
  - name: Logistics & Resources
    description: Fuel caches, island depots, and offshore platforms serve as resupply nodes. Convoys must navigate beach approaches and avoid ambush-prone mangrove corridors.
  deployment: A fixed deployment budget (~10,000 points) forces players to choose between naval dominance, air superiority, or distributed amphibious mobility. Blue deploys from the southwest offshore staging platform; Red deploys from the northeast cliffside command island.
  ar:
    viewingDistance: "~4\u20135 m"
    physicalArea: "10\xD710 m"
    representedArea: "~1 km\xB2"
    scale: 1:100
    fov: "~53\xB0 diagonal"
    resolution: "1920\xD71080 per eye"
    tracking: Inside-out tracking detects horizontal planes. Depth-mesh (if available) provides limited occlusion.
    interaction: Virtual objects render over real-world view; assume minimal real-world occlusion.
  coordinateSystem: "1000\xD71000 grid (1 unit \u2248 1 m). Origin (0,0) = southwest corner."
  keyLocations:
  - name: Blue HQ (Offshore Staging Platform)
    coordinate: (0,0)
    sizeOrElevation: "150\xD7150 m"
    description: Naval docks, drone pads, amphibious armor staging.
  - name: Red HQ (Cliffside Command Island)
    coordinate: (1000,1000)
    sizeOrElevation: "150\xD7150 m"
    description: Hardened cliff bunker with radar mast, AA emplacements, and sonar arrays.
  - name: Central Island Cluster
    coordinate: (500,450)
    sizeOrElevation: "350\xD7300 m"
    description: Three mid-sized islands with beaches, cliffs, and villages.
  - name: Island Depot & Village
    coordinate: (250,800)
    sizeOrElevation: "120\xD7120 m"
    description: Supply huts, docks, interior flanking routes.
  - name: Mangrove Swamp Network
    coordinate: (800,300)
    sizeOrElevation: "200\xD7200 m"
    description: Dense vegetation, shallow water, stealth movement.
  - name: Deep-Water Channel
    coordinate: "(0,450 \u2192 400,900)"
    sizeOrElevation: Primary naval chokepoint
    description: Layered defenses and coral hazards.
  - name: Cliffside Trail Route
    coordinate: "(300,0 \u2192 450,350)"
    sizeOrElevation: Route
    description: Safer land route with partial cover.
  - name: Cliff Relay A
    coordinate: (650,150)
    sizeOrElevation: +240 m
    description: Long-range sensor vantage point.
  - name: Cliff Relay B
    coordinate: (150,650)
    sizeOrElevation: +260 m
    description: Comms relay hub and sonar control node.
  - name: Neutral Forward Outpost
    coordinate: (500,950)
    sizeOrElevation: Outpost
    description: Drone resupply zone.
  chokepointsAndSightlines:
  - name: Deep-Water Channel
    description: Major naval chokepoint; controlling it determines sea movement.
  - name: Mangrove Swamp Network
    description: Interior flanking routes; stealthy but slow.
  - name: Central Island Cluster
    description: Multi-node combat zone; ideal for distributed warfare.
  - name: Cliffside Trail
    description: Predictable but safe; vulnerable to overwatch from cliffs.
  - name: Sightlines
    description: Cliff Relay A provides long-range sensor coverage (~350 m). Sea spray and humidity create fog-of-war pockets.
  terrain: Beaches, cliffs, coral shelves, mangroves, offshore platforms, island villages.
  vegetation: Palm trees, mangroves, shrubs, beach grass.
  buildingsAndProps: 'Military: AA guns, radar dishes, sonar arrays, bunkers. Industrial: Docks, generators, pipelines. Logistics: Ships, cargo crates, fuel drums, drones.'
  effects: Sea spray, fog, humidity haze, wave impacts, thermal distortion.
  audio: Waves, wind, ship engines, sonar pings, radio chatter.
  lodBudget:
  - category: Coral/Terrain
    count: 3
    trianglesPerItem: 200000
    totalTriangles: 600000
  - category: Naval/Industrial
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 80000
    totalTriangles: 320000
  - category: Buildings/Military
    count: 15
    trianglesPerItem: 50000
    totalTriangles: 750000
  - category: Roads/Paths
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 30000
    totalTriangles: 120000
  - category: Props
    count: 50
    trianglesPerItem: 10000
    totalTriangles: 500000
  textureBudget: "2048\xB2 for terrain/buildings, 1024\xB2 for props. DXT1/5 compression. Target \u2264100 MB."
  engineAndPlugins: Unreal ARTemplate + Nreal SDK (XREAL). ARKit/ARCore enabled.
  rendering: Forward renderer, stationary lights, baked GI, aggressive culling.
  anchors: Single spatial anchor for entire map.
  interaction: Phone pointer for pan/zoom; HUD as screen-space widgets.
  multiplayer: Client-server architecture; offload AI/physics to server.
  milestones:
  - name: "Prototype Layout \u2014 Month 1"
    description: Block-out islands, reefs, mangroves, AR anchor test.
  - name: "Core Systems \u2014 Month 2"
    description: NavMesh (sea + land), amphibious autonomy, distributed node logic.
  - name: "AR Integration \u2014 Month 3"
    description: Anchors, plane detection, basic interactivity.
  - name: "Content Fill \u2014 Month 4\u20135"
    description: Final models, textures, lighting, audio.
  - name: "Gameplay & Polish \u2014 Month 6\u20137"
    description: Objectives, balance, VFX (sea spray, fog, thermal distortion).
  - name: "Testing & QA \u2014 Month 8"
    description: Multiplayer stress test, sensor validation.
  testing:
  - name: Autonomy
    description: Verify naval routing, amphibious landings, distributed node coordination.
  - name: Comms/Sensors
    description: Test relay destruction, fog-of-war updates, sonar interference.
  - name: Performance
    description: "\u226560 Hz AR render on target device."
  - name: QA Checklist
    description: Navigation, amphibious logic, distributed objective behavior, anchor drift, sensor accuracy.
